  "description": "Faithful replication (survey stage) of Krupiński, Rusnak, Żagan, Kuczyński, Koszewicz, Szmigiel & Geniusz (2025), Composition and Contrast: The Painterly Nature of Architectural Exterior Illumination, Arts 14(6):139. Three computer simulations of the floodlit façade of a neoclassical building complex differ only in where luminance contrast falls (A: distant central part brighter, B: closer wings brighter, C: even), at the same average luminance of 10 cd/m². Participants, in a dark room, see all variants together and choose which they like most and least, which is calmest, and which best conveys official character, makes the building look wider and creates the strongest depth.",
